<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yermak Timofeyevich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from <a href="/years/1581">1581</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yermak Timofeyevich was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> leader who led an expedition across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-mountains">Ural Mountains</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> in the 1580s, defeating the Khanate of Sibir. His campaigns from 1581 onward opened the way for Russian expansion across northern Asia. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> treat them as the start of the eastward expansion that eventually carried Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> to the Pacific.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yermak-timofeyevich.jpg" alt="Yermak Timofeyevich" width="303" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yermak_Timofeyevich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
